    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'BoxCutter allows you to inject your own custom code into its connection
    logic.


    In this example, the standard require logic would normally cause
    the entire rig to collapse when more than one leg is disconnected. However, by
    enabling canCusRequireLogic and assigning a custom MonoBehaviour for logic injection,
    the four-legged creature remains standing.


    Refer to the documentation for
    details on creating and integrating your own custom logic.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: c2f197c1fd09ef44b9e81d34868385df, type: 2}
